# U-8 ClientHello fixtures — where each byte came from.
# Reference-device captures are the plan's §12.1 requirement (fixture B/C "Chrome-stable
# capture"); A is generated, B/C/D are real captures (B/C on the X6532, D on the API 37 image).

fixture_a_example_com.bin
source=python3 ssl.MemoryBIO wrap_bio(server_hostname="example.com"); do_handshake(); read outgoing BIO
retrieved_at=2026-09-20
client=CPython 3.x (host)
notes=no ECH extension; parser verdict Sni("example.com")
sha256=1aa6af76ae958fe200f6e9bb82ab12c7c3a6c619ce93cfae209d6a6ccf0942ce

fixture_b_chrome_pq.bin
source=scripts/domainusage-tls-hello-capture.py 9445 /tmp/hello-capture (host listener), Chrome to https://du-b.192.0.2.99.nip.io:9445
retrieved_at=2026-09-21
device=Infinix X6532 (reference low-end, Android 14 / API 34)
client=Chrome 153.0.8010.47 (Android)
notes=hello-01.bin of 20; arrived as two TCP segments, 1448 B + 546 B (pcap /tmp/du-fixture-b.pcap);
      carries X25519MLKEM768 key share and 0xFE0D (GREASE ECH, 250 B payload — the target
      publishes no HTTPS RR with an ECH config), so the parser verdict is Ech and the plaintext
      SNI (du-b.192.0.2.99.nip.io, a spec-mandated public name) is ignored.
      At publication the embedded SNI IP was rewritten to a TEST-NET-1 documentation address
      (same length, so the SNI length byte and file size are unchanged).
sha256=595b6b7b3527977233a4ec71123d3e54330823978f614d2febbec60fd22e88c3

fixture_c_chrome_ech.bin
source=scripts/domainusage-tls-hello-capture.py (same session as fixture B)
retrieved_at=2026-09-21
device=Infinix X6532 (reference low-end, Android 14 / API 34)
client=Chrome 153.0.8010.47 (Android)
notes=hello-06.bin of 20; smallest ECH extension in the session (186 B, plausible-config shape);
      all 20 captures carried 0xFE0D, so no real Chrome hello without ECH existed to capture.
      RFC 9849 §6.2 makes GREASE indistinguishable from a real config by design.
      At publication the embedded SNI IP was rewritten to a TEST-NET-1 documentation address
      (same length, so the SNI length byte and file size are unchanged).
sha256=08a2ea18f9e123167a7688d698789febfa77010794e4d521b0f7aa051c4865d2

fixture_d_android17_ech.bin
source=scripts/domainusage-tls-hello-capture.py 9447 /tmp/hello-capture-api37 (host listener), Chrome to https://du-b.10.0.2.2.nip.io:9447
retrieved_at=2026-09-29
device=MyExodus_API37 AVD (sdk_gphone64_x86_64, Android 17 / API 37) — the ECH-by-default
       reference target; replaces the earlier synthetic stand-in.
client=Chrome 145.0.7632.218 (Android)
notes=hello-03.bin of 3 (captured after `pm clear com.android.chrome` + first-run dismissal);
      smallest ECH extension in the session (186 B — same convention as fixture C). Carries
      GREASE + X25519MLKEM768 (group 0x11EC) + X25519 key shares and 0xFE0D (GREASE ECH — the
      target publishes no HTTPS RR), so the parser verdict is Ech and the plaintext SNI
      (du-b.10.0.2.2.nip.io, a spec-mandated public name) is ignored. Accompanies the I-12b
      device leg (Chrome -> tls-ech.dev, sni_ech counter) on the same image.
sha256=04ec8c93fe2a92166e406c65fe07cf72df15615828807ebc85b80bcd2a733503
